GLM-5.3 with gr8 on four DGX Sparks (TP4)

Repository-authored patches, scripts, configuration and documentation: MIT, see LICENSE.

patches/ modifies kindlingai/gr8 (https://github.com/kindlingai/gr8) at
6448a16661abd81e9540bc073b3cfa92d7234565. gr8 is MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 gr8 engine
contributors; its licence is retained in LICENSES/MIT-gr8.txt and applies to the
upstream code the patches touch. The patches do not remove or alter any upstream
copyright or licence notice.

The Dockerfile builds from upstream gr8 sources fetched at build time and uses the
upstream image ghcr.io/kindlingai/gr8, pinned by digest, as its base. No container
image is distributed here; the referenced images keep their own terms, including
NVIDIA's CUDA base images.

No model weights are distributed, and the MIT licence above does not cover any.
kindlingai/glm-5.3-exlr8-k2-k3-k4 is under the GLM-5.3 licence (Z.ai,
https://huggingface.co/zai-org/GLM-5.3/blob/main/LICENSE) plus CC BY 4.0 for the
quantization additions (see its model card). incoai/GLM-5.3-DFlash2 is
CC BY-NC-ND 4.0 (noncommercial): it is not included, modified or redistributed;
each user downloads it and upstream gr8 converts it locally, which does not lift
the noncommercial restriction.

RigMark (alexellis/rigmark) is credited as the benchmark; none of its code is
included. See CREDITS.md.
